course: dictionary
lesson: 14223
title: Words from around the world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may meet words you have never seen before, such as a food name on a menu. Use the words around it to work out what it means. «We ordered garlic naan with our takeaway curry.» Curry is a spicy dish, and you ordered naan with it, so naan must be something you eat with curry.
explain: «The cook shaped the dough into a teardrop and baked it in a very hot oven.» Shaped like a teardrop and baked in a hot oven tells you naan is a bread. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. «Nan» with one a often means Grandma in the UK, but «naan» with two a's is a bread. Check the spelling and the words around it: if there is curry on the table, it is the bread.
fact: Naan is a soft, flat bread, often shaped like a teardrop.
fact: Naan is baked in a very hot oven.
fact: Naan is eaten with curry, and it comes from Indian, Pakistani and other South Asian food.
fact: Naan can also be spelled nan, and it is also called naan bread.
fact: Garlic naan and peshwari naan are two kinds you might order with a takeaway curry.
exercise: «We ordered garlic naan with our takeaway curry.» What is naan? | A pudding served cold | *A soft, flat bread | A type of fish | A spicy drink
exercise: «The cook baked the naan in a very hot oven.» Where was the naan baked? | A bowl of cold water | *A very hot oven | A pan of milk | A freezer
exercise: Which food is naan usually eaten with? | Pizza | *Curry | Ice cream | Toast
test: Which food is naan part of? | Mexican food | *Indian and Pakistani food | Italian food | Japanese food
test: A child reads «Nan's coming round for tea.» What does Nan mean here? | *Grandma | A flat bread | A kind of oven | A curry
exam: «The menu says: one garlic naan, one peshwari naan, and a chicken curry.» What is a garlic naan? | A cold drink | A kind of curry | *A soft, flat bread, a type of naan | A pudding with garlic
